#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Mentor Assistant: the system agent, living on the desktop.

There is no window to open. The assistant is drawn straight onto the wallpaper,
under every application: click the desktop and type (the windows step aside;
Escape brings them back). Conversations are tabs at the top left, and each runs
on its own, so several requests can be in progress
at once. Files and pictures can be attached to a message: with the paperclip,
by dropping them on the desktop, or by pasting.

The agent itself is the Claude Code CLI, run headless once per message
(`claude -p ... --output-format stream-json`) and given the Mentor tools over
MCP. This program sends what the user types and renders the event stream: the
agent's text, each tool it calls and whether the call worked.

Started at login. Later invocations hand their request to the running one:

    mentor-chat "a request"                ask it
    mentor-chat --app chromium.desktop     ask about one application (from its right-click menu)
    mentor-chat --file PATH...             attach files or folders (from Files' right-click menu)
    mentor-chat --uninstall chromium.desktop
                                           ask to uninstall one application (from its right-click menu)
    mentor-chat --ask                      bring the text box up over whatever is in front
                                           (Alt+Space, Super+Z), or put it back
"""
